{{Elections in Kentucky}}

The '''1990 United States Senate election in Kentucky''' was held on November 6, 1990. Incumbent [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] U.S. Senator [[Mitch McConnell]] won re-election to a second term.

==Republican primary ==
===Candidates ===
* [[Mitch McConnell]], incumbent U.S. Senator
* Tommy Klein, perennial candidate

